#### [MODIFY] [ProductImage.java](file:///c:/Users/jadha/.gemini/antigravity/playground/mrsdeore/backend/src/main/java/com/mrsdeores/models/ProductImage.java)
- Add `publicId` (`@Column(name="public_id")`)
- Add `resourceType` (`@Column(name="resource_type")`, default `"image"`)

#### [MODIFY] [Category.java](file:///c:/Users/jadha/.gemini/antigravity/playground/mrsdeore/backend/src/main/java/com/mrsdeores/models/Category.java)
- Same two fields.

---

### [Backend] Deletion Lifecycle

#### [MODIFY] CategoryController + ProductController
- **On Update (image replaced):** `cloudinaryService.deleteMedia(oldPublicId, oldResourceType)` called **only after** DB save success. If delete fails → log + skip (no crash).
- **On Entity Delete:** Same delete-after-save pattern.
- **Orphan Strategy:** New `OrphanCleanupService` with `@Scheduled(cron="0 0 3 * * SUN")` weekly scan — finds `product_images`/`categories` rows with `public_id` not matching any known Cloudinary asset and logs them for manual review.

---

### [Frontend] Upload Service

#### [NEW] cloudinaryUploadService.ts
- `uploadToCloudinary(file: File, mediaType: MediaTypeEnum, entityId?: number)`
  1. Validate file type client-side (first line of defense)
  2. `POST /api/media/signature` → signed params
  3. Build [FormData](file:///c:/Users/jadha/.gemini/antigravity/playground/mrsdeore/frontend/src/components/ProductForm.tsx#15-27) with [file](file:///c:/Users/jadha/.gemini/antigravity/playground/mrsdeore/backend/Dockerfile) + all signed params
  4. `POST https://api.cloudinary.com/v1_1/{cloudName}/{resourceType}/upload` directly
  5. Returns `{ secureUrl, publicId, resourceType }`
- Resource type → upload URL mapping is fully dynamic based on `mediaType`.

---

### [Frontend] Component Refactoring

#### [MODIFY] [AdminCategories.tsx](file:///c:/Users/jadha/.gemini/antigravity/playground/mrsdeore/frontend/src/pages/AdminCategories.tsx)
- Replace `api.post('/upload', formData)` with `cloudinaryUploadService.uploadToCloudinary(file, 'CATEGORY')`
- Store `publicId` alongside `imageUrl` in state; send both to backend on save.
- Use lazy loading on `<img>` tags (`loading="lazy"`).

#### [MODIFY] [ProductForm.tsx](file:///c:/Users/jadha/.gemini/antigravity/playground/mrsdeore/frontend/src/components/ProductForm.tsx)
- Same refactor; `mediaType='PRODUCT'` + `entityId=product.id`.

